1
00:00:00,659 --> 00:00:07,919
Small organizations copy facts from emails and letters into forms.

2
00:00:07,959 --> 00:00:15,610
AI can fill forms, but you can't tell what's real, guessed, or quietly picked.

3
00:00:15,650 --> 00:00:23,210
TraceForm fills forms with Meta's Muse Spark, and every answer shows its proof.

4
00:00:23,250 --> 00:00:31,839
The sample: three fictional documents. One is a Word file.

5
00:00:31,879 --> 00:00:39,900
Run live: the documents go to Meta's Muse Spark (muse-spark-1.3).

6
00:00:39,940 --> 00:00:44,960
Schema-constrained JSON: every field needs a verbatim quote, or stays empty.

7
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:49,853
Schema-constrained JSON: every field needs a verbatim quote, or stays empty.
[Sped up 4×. Real wait: 24 s]

8
00:00:49,893 --> 00:00:56,353
Live result. Code, not the model, checks that each quote is in the source.

9
00:00:56,393 --> 00:01:02,092
Nothing is approved until a person approves it.

10
00:01:02,132 --> 00:01:11,692
Click a field: the exact sentence is highlighted, with its citation number.

11
00:01:11,732 --> 00:01:22,416
Checks: code found the quote. A second Meta call gives an advisory opinion.

12
00:01:22,456 --> 00:01:29,816
Sources disagree: $48,000 in the application, $54,000 in a later email.

13
00:01:29,856 --> 00:01:35,016
TraceForm shows both quotes and doesn't pick a side.

14
00:01:35,056 --> 00:01:42,068
The person chooses $54,000 and approves it.

15
00:01:42,108 --> 00:01:50,629
Not in any document? It stays blank. Nothing is guessed.

16
00:01:50,669 --> 00:01:56,229
Now the Sample data run: a hand-made fixture, not live AI.

17
00:01:56,269 --> 00:02:01,429
It contains one planted fake quote. Code couldn't find it in the source.

18
00:02:01,469 --> 00:02:06,229
Meta's model got one repair pass: re-cite word for word, or give up.

19
00:02:06,269 --> 00:02:11,091
Live test: 3/3 fake citations caught. 2 re-cited, the fake one withdrawn.

20
00:02:11,131 --> 00:02:21,291
Photos and scans are read by Muse Spark vision, and labeled that way.

21
00:02:21,331 --> 00:02:32,115
Quotes are verified against that text. Compare it with the original.

22
00:02:32,155 --> 00:02:42,892
Export the reviewed values as CSV or JSON.

23
00:02:42,932 --> 00:02:47,709
The chosen $54,000 is in the file, marked as approved by a person.

24
00:02:47,749 --> 00:02:54,219
Meta's model reads, extracts, repairs, double-checks. Code verifies. A person decides.
